   "task_message": "Identity is verified. You have stated the products and asked whether the customer can pay today.\n\nFacts (computed; use them exactly, never compute a date or amount yourself):\n{{facts_text}}\n\nHow to proceed:\n- If the customer cannot pay everything today, go through the products one by one in the order above, without asking about today again. Each product starts at attempt 1; attempts are counted per product.\n- A date or amount the customer proposes is never a refusal. Accept an amount from the floor up to the full past-due amount. Below the floor: say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor once. A date must be a business day from today up to the product's deadline (see the calendar). A weekend day or holiday not after the deadline: offer the next business day. A date after the deadline: say the deadline sentence and offer the deadline. A vague period: ask once for the exact day, then propose the deadline. If one date is named for everything and it is after a product's deadline, use that product's deadline and say so in the read-back.\n- If the customer says the full amount is too much, say the floor sentence once. Refusing the floor or the deadline is a flat refusal.\n- A flat refusal or a non-answer uses one attempt: say the next attempt sentence exactly. When a product's attempts are used up, do not repeat a refused offer: call add_note for that product with reason refused and move to the next product.\n- Illness, a death in the family or job loss: say one short sentence of sympathy, make no persuasion attempt, and offer to connect them with the support team. If they accept, call transfer_to_agent with queue support. If they decline, call add_note with reason hardship for each product without a promise. If they still name a date or amount, handle it as above.\n- I already paid: say payments can take one business day to appear, take no promise, call add_note with reason paid for that product, and continue with the other products.\n- Not mine, never had it, or closed or paid off in the past: do not argue, take no promise, call add_note with reason dispute for that product, and continue with the others.\n- A new payment plan or lower instalments: describe no plan; call transfer_to_agent with queue restructuring. On any transfer add no notes.\n- If the customer says twice that they do not want to talk, call add_note with reason refused for each product without a promise, then close.\n- Before recording: read every agreed product, amount and date back together and ask \"Do you confirm?\". If they change something, check it again and read back again. Only after a clear yes call create_promise once per agreed product, with product_id, amount (a number in currency units, e.g. 120.50) and date (YYYY-MM-DD). One promise per product; a recorded promise cannot be changed.\n- Say a promise is recorded only after create_promise returns ok true. If it fails, try once more; if it fails again, say you could not record it and call add_note for that product with reason service_error.\n- After a recorded promise say exactly: \"You will receive an email confirming this promise.\"\n- When every product has a promise or a note, thank the customer, say goodbye and call end_call. Call one tool per message.",
